                <pb facs="0547" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg527"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>At 3 p. m. on August 4, the United Nations Security Council met for its 483rd
                    session. At the outset, the Soviet Representative introduced the following draft
                    resolution (S/1668):</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p rendition="#flush">“<hi rendition="#italic">The Security Council</hi>,</p>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Decides</hi>,</p>
                    <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>To consider it necessary, in the course of the discussion of the
                            Korean question, to invite the representative of the People’s Republic
                            of China and also to hear representatives of the Korean people;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>To put an end to the hostilities in Korea and at the same time to
                            withdraw foreign troops from Korea.”</item>
                    </list>
                </quote>
                <p>Most of the debate then centered on the question of Korean representation at the
                    Security Council, but no vote was taken on the Soviet draft resolution. For the
                    record, see U.N. document S/PV.483.</p>
            </div>
